		{
			dependencies: ["2ECFF275EF74DA42"]
			description: [
				"Approach ruins slowly, photograph or mark the site, and search for suspicious blocks before flattening the area. Brushes recover information that a pickaxe destroys."
				"Keep pottery, relics and written clues together until their purpose is understood. An apparently useless fragment may identify a structure, collection or later crafting path."
				"Restore one section of a ruin instead of stripping every block. The world feels richer when discoveries leave a visible history behind."
				"Better Archeology expands suspicious sand and gravel into a broader field practice with fossils, ruins, artifact shards, and analysis. Bring several brushes, light, scaffolding blocks, and empty protected inventory slots."
			]
			id: "6D04014F7539F025"
